@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
top to bottom direction
title Target: UI DAG through Wayang to multiple Rust nodes
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam ArrowColor #34536F
skinparam nodeBackgroundColor #F3F6FA
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D6

actor User
component "OpenTSx UI\nexisting DAG editor" as ui
node "Control plane" {
  component "SaaS admission\nplanned capability + policy checks" as backend
  component "Wayang driver / site platform\nplanned fragment placement + fanout" as driver
  component "ExecutionAssignments\nimplemented Java preflight" as java
  database "Durable deployment journal\nplanned generations + delivery cursor" as journal
}
node "Site A / Rust node A" {
  component "tsx-runner\nplanned operator execution + checkpoint" as runnerA
  component "tsx-contracts\nimplemented Rust preflight" as contractsA
}
node "Site B / Rust node B" {
  component "tsx-runner\nplanned operator execution + checkpoint" as runnerB
  component "tsx-contracts\nimplemented Rust preflight" as contractsB
}
database "Approved Kafka channels\nexplicit bindings + partition ownership" as topics

User --> ui
ui --> backend : original DAG
backend --> driver : admitted deployment request
driver --> java : validate assignment set
driver --> journal : prepare / activate / retire
driver --> runnerA : fragment + partition set A
driver --> runnerB : fragment + partition set B
runnerA --> contractsA : validate envelope
runnerB --> contractsB : validate envelope
runnerA <--> topics : assigned channels
runnerB <--> topics : assigned channels

note bottom of java
Offline schema, hash, offset and overlap checks exist.
They do not authorize execution or fence live writers.
end note
note bottom of topics
First prototype uses static ownership.
Every cross-node edge needs an admitted data channel.
Raw records do not pass through the driver.
end note
@enduml
